        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T18:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The CL that adds a \u0027message wait response\u0027 state does convert both mode_entry and mode_exit functions into a boolean helper function that when it returns true will cause it to switch to the \u0027message wait response\u0027 state.\n\nData Reset can\u0027t use the same message wait response state because Data Resets can involve multiple PE states (e.g. VCONN swaps are required). So really the mode_entry/exit helper functions need to return 3 values.\n\n1. false -\u003e no action\n2. true -\u003e switch to Data Reset state\n3. true -\u003e switch to message wait state\n\nThe mode_entry/exit functions could be converted to return an enum instead of a bool so both true cases can be handled.",
      "parentUuid": "172c1c6e_7d36be1c",
      "revId": "3b6bb6fe5d311d0f915c98f6124a01c08f3afc9a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
